# SRG-APP-000785-AU-000200  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement a report generation capability that
# does not alter original content or time ordering of audit records.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000785-AU-000200
group:           V-263566
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003829
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    A Splunk report is a search over indexed records, so content and ordering
                 in the report are governed by the report's own search string and by the
                 search-time settings applied to the source types it reads - all
                 application configuration.

governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           field_filters.conf [<fieldFilterName>] action absent
check:           props.conf [<source type>] SEDCMD-<class> absent
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search matches tls1\.2
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*ssl3
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.0
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether the rendered report preserves content and time ordering is
                 confirmed by comparing report output against the stored records, which the
                 assessor performs.
external:        Handling of an exported report after it leaves the application -
                 re-sorted, edited or excerpted downstream - rests on the recipient's
                 procedures.

citation:        field_filters.conf.spec:32 [<fieldFilterName>], :37-70 action operator
                 vocabulary; props.conf.spec:80 [<spec>], :1243 SEDCMD-<class>, :1313
                 EVAL-<fieldname>; savedsearches.conf.spec:44 search.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: a field filter or SEDCMD class
                 applies to the audit data a report reads, or the report's own search
                 rewrites field values, so the application's report generation capability
                 does not present the original content of the audit records.
